      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, you are absolutely right to be worried about how promptly his fatigue could improve, but loading him with a massive dose of iron supplements right now is dangerous. While iron isn't a slow-acting vitamin, taking double the standard dose at once can cause severe nausea, vomiting, or even life-threatening toxicity in a teenager, and it does not necessarily replenish stores any faster in the short term. The most effective and safest way to actually speed up recovery is to follow his doctor's prescribed dosing schedule exactly, which usually avoids these harsh side effects while still delivering the iron your son needs.",
